<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gümüştekin Gazi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1134</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Gazi Gümüştekin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gümüştekin Gazi was the Danishmendid emir from about 1104 to 1134, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danishmend-gazi">Danishmend Gazi</a>. He held the crusader Bohemond of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> captive until 1103, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malatya">Malatya</a> in 1103 and fought both the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> and the crusader states. The Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> granted him the title malik, and for a time he was the strongest Turkish ruler in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>.</p></div>
